Ok. I think that the amulet is nice, but not too nice. It doesn't
massively improve survivability (allows to avoid about 10% of deaths
between Oracle and Castle IME; an early wish, a convenient altar and
the like can account for much more) and thus getting the amulet
instead of the bag - or instead of getting neither - doesn't give a
game-breaking advantage. I remain unconvinced that the option for the
amulet needs to be removed or "balanced".

It can be argued that one of two objects which are definite
ascension-kit material are guaranteed to turn up as shallow (and as
easy to acquire) as that, but then both ought to be removed, not only
one. Give an oilskin sack and an amulet of ESP instead.

